THE SHORT VERSION

This repository is public so that people can read the code — to judge the work,
to learn from it, or to decide whether to hire me. It is not open source. You
may read it. You may not use it.

Some of what is in here is not mine to license to you at all. See THIRD-PARTY
CONTENT below, because that part matters more than the rest.


WHAT YOU MAY DO

- Read the source code.
- Quote short extracts in a review, article or teaching material, with
  attribution.
- Fork it on GitHub for the purpose of reading it or proposing a change back.


WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO WITHOUT WRITTEN PERMISSION

- Use this code, in whole or in part, in any other project, commercial or not.
- Copy the design, layout, stylesheets or templates into another site or
  application.
- Redistribute, republish, sell, sublicense or host this software.
- Train a model on this repository as a substantial part of its corpus.
- Remove or alter this notice.


THIRD-PARTY CONTENT — NOT LICENSED, NOT MINE TO GIVE

Parts of this repository are other people's work. They are included here with
permission for use in ThaiBridge AI only, or under the terms of their own
licence. My permission does not extend to them, and nothing in this file grants
you any right to use them:

- Essays by Pra Kru Samu Panya Vajiro, written by him and published here with
  his consent for this site. His words, his copyright.
- Transcribed chant texts from a printed chanting book. The book's own
  copyright applies to its contents, typesetting and editorial material.
- Dhamma talks and readings attributed to their respective teachers.
- Teacher-recorded and generated audio in static/audio/, recorded or produced
  for this project.
- Dictionary data derived from third-party sources, which carry their own
  licence terms.

If you are extracting anything from this repository for any purpose, assume the
content is not available to you and ask first.


